---
description: Tiny Factory Rush XR project operating rules
alwaysApply: true
---

Read AGENTS.md before changing the project.

For XR/product work also read:
- docs/xr/PRODUCT_THESIS.md
- docs/xr/ROADMAP.md
- docs/xr/DECISIONS.md
- docs/xr/COMPETITION_SCORECARD.md

Rules:
- game first; industrial engineering stays in system rules, not academic vocabulary;
- tabletop MR, hands-first end-to-end;
- interpret hand intent; do not copy gestures/timing constants from other games;
- visible consequences over dashboards;
- build a runnable walking skeleton before perfecting architecture;
- art/audio/pitch progress in parallel with gameplay;
- signature interaction = player verb; overflow = possible crisis/magic moment; rhythm = feedback;
- one polished core before optional stretch;
- optional stretch is owner-authorized, never automatic;
- do not add workers, detailed safety/quality/maintenance, multiplayer, agentic AI, online leaderboard or complex supply chain without an accepted owner decision/task;
- preserve pre-competition Git history;
- never claim simulator evidence is Quest evidence;
- never claim a test passed unless actually run;
- protected product/governance files may not be changed by autonomous implementation agents;
- after the v1.0 design freeze, product changes require measured evidence, official-rule changes or a documented competitor event.
